From: mscharged-port
Subject: Admit the original in-game frame updates under the match-loading diagnostic
Upstream-base: efa6fc84680e48bfdca7e6ac245d8abf333ae617

E13 admission of original BeginFrameTask::Run blocks that the frontend task
diagnostic omits, under the explicit MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_MATCH_LOADING
profile only: hiding the two shadow-volume layer views, the game Presentation
and NisPlayer update in states 0x2001B, the per-character frame update, the
depth-of-field turn-off outside states 0x18, and the co-planar reference /
particle in-front / safe-frame / grid block. Without the Presentation update
the original "GameBegin" presentation never completes, so
FixedUpdateTask::mSimulationStarted stays false and the match never kicks off.
The bodies are unchanged original source; the HOME-button render and the debug
screenshot request remain omitted (HOME is internally owned). Matching
depthoffield.cpp declares PSMTXIdentity itself, outside the SDK header, so its
native build applies the same PSMTXIdentity -> C_MTXIdentity alias as
revolution/mtx/mtx.h.

diff --git a/src/Game/Render/depthoffield.cpp b/src/Game/Render/depthoffield.cpp
--- a/src/Game/Render/depthoffield.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Render/depthoffield.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,10 @@ extern "C"
     void GXProject(float x, float y, float z, const Mtx matrix,
         const float* projection, const float* viewport, float* screenX,
         float* screenY, float* screenZ);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// As in revolution/mtx/mtx.h, the native SDK supplies the C matrix routine.
+#define PSMTXIdentity C_MTXIdentity
+#endif
     void PSMTXIdentity(Mtx matrix);
     void* memcpy(void* destination, const void* source, u32 size);
 }
